---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy — IKIAN Dimitsana"
  description="Privacy Policy for IKIAN Dimitsana boutique suites. Learn how we protect your personal data."
>
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="container text-center">
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <div class="divider"></div>
      <p class="page-subtitle">Last updated: September 25, 2025</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section legal-content">
    <div class="container legal-container">

      <!--
        PRIVACY POLICY TEMPLATE
        =======================
        This privacy policy has been drafted for a privacy-first, cookie-free static website.
        It follows a conservative EU GDPR + ePrivacy approach.

        TODO: LEGAL REVIEW REQUIRED — This template must be reviewed by a qualified legal
        professional before publication. Items marked TODO require business-specific details.
      -->

      <p class="legal-intro">
        IKIAN Dimitsana ("we", "us", "our") is committed to protecting your privacy.
        This Privacy Policy explains what personal data we collect, why we collect it,
        how we use it, and your rights under the General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR)
        and applicable Greek law.
      </p>

      <h2>1. Data Controller</h2>
      <p>
        The data controller responsible for your personal data is:
      </p>
      <p>
        <!-- TODO: Replace with full legal entity name and registration details -->
        <strong>IKIAN Dimitsana</strong><br>
        Dimitsana, Arcadia, Greece<br>
        Email: <a href="mailto:ikian.dimitsana@gmail.com">ikian.dimitsana@gmail.com</a><br>
        Phone: <a href="tel:+306973373560">+30 697 337 3560</a>
      </p>
      <!-- TODO: Add VAT number / business registration number if applicable -->

      <h2>2. What Personal Data We Collect</h2>

      <h3>2.1 When you contact us</h3>
      <p>
        If you contact us by phone or email, we may collect:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Your name</li>
        <li>Email address</li>
        <li>Phone number</li>
        <li>The content of your message</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        <strong>Lawful basis:</strong> Legitimate interest (to respond to your enquiry)
        and/or pre-contractual measures (Article 6(1)(b) GDPR).
      </p>

      <h3>2.2 When you make a reservation</h3>
      <p>
        For bookings made directly (by phone, email, or bank transfer), we collect:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Full name</li>
        <li>Contact details (phone number, email address)</li>
        <li>ID card number, passport number, or Tax Identification Number (AFM) — as required by Greek guest registry law</li>
        <li>Payment details (bank transfer reference)</li>
        <li>Dates of stay</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        <strong>Lawful basis:</strong> Performance of a contract (Article 6(1)(b) GDPR)
        and legal obligation — compliance with Greek guest registry requirements (Article 6(1)(c) GDPR).
      </p>

      <h3>2.3 When you book via Airbnb</h3>
      <p>
        If you book through Airbnb, your booking data is processed by Airbnb Ireland UC
        under its own privacy policy. We receive only the information necessary to fulfil
        your reservation. Please refer to
        <a href="https://www.airbnb.com/terms/privacy_policy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
          Airbnb's Privacy Policy
        </a> for details.
      </p>

      <h2>3. This Website — Privacy by Design</h2>
      <p>
        This website has been designed with privacy as a core principle:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>No cookies</strong> are set by this website.</li>
        <li><strong>No analytics or tracking</strong> scripts are loaded (no Google Analytics, Meta Pixel, Hotjar, or similar).</li>
        <li><strong>No third-party fonts</strong> are loaded — we use system fonts only.</li>
        <li><strong>No third-party CDN assets</strong> — all resources are self-hosted.</li>
        <li><strong>No embedded third-party widgets</strong> (no chat widgets, no embedded maps, no social media plugins).</li>
        <li><strong>No cookie consent banner</strong> is needed because no non-essential cookies or trackers are used.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        The only external links on this website are to Airbnb (for booking) and OpenStreetMap
        (for directions). Clicking these links will take you to third-party websites governed
        by their own privacy policies.
      </p>

      <h2>4. Web Server Logs</h2>
      <p>
        Our web hosting provider may automatically collect standard server access logs, which can include:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>IP address</li>
        <li>Date and time of access</li>
        <li>Pages requested</li>
        <li>Browser type and operating system</li>
        <li>Referring URL</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        <strong>Lawful basis:</strong> Legitimate interest — ensuring the security, integrity,
        and proper functioning of the website (Article 6(1)(f) GDPR).
      </p>
      <!-- TODO: Confirm with hosting provider what logs are kept and the retention period -->
      <p>
        Server logs are retained for a limited period for security purposes and are not used
        for tracking or profiling visitors.
      </p>

      <h2>5. How We Use Your Data</h2>
      <p>We use your personal data only for the following purposes:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>To respond to your enquiries</li>
        <li>To process and manage your reservation</li>
        <li>To comply with legal obligations (guest registry, tax records)</li>
        <li>To protect the security of our property and website</li>
      </ul>
      <p>We do <strong>not</strong> use your data for marketing, profiling, automated decision-making, or selling to third parties.</p>

      <h2>6. Data Sharing</h2>
      <p>
        Your personal data is not shared with third parties except:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Where required by Greek law (e.g., guest registry submissions to authorities)</li>
        <li>With our web hosting provider (for server infrastructure only)</li>
        <!-- TODO: List any other data processors if applicable (e.g., accountant, booking platform) -->
      </ul>
      <p>
        We do not sell, rent, or trade your personal data.
      </p>

      <h2>7. Data Retention</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Enquiry data:</strong> Retained for up to 12 months, then deleted.</li>
        <li><strong>Guest registry data:</strong> Retained as required by Greek law.</li>
        <li><strong>Financial records:</strong> Retained as required by Greek tax law.</li>
        <!-- TODO: Confirm specific legal retention periods with a legal advisor -->
      </ul>

      <h2>8. Your Rights</h2>
      <p>
        Under the GDPR, you have the following rights regarding your personal data:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Right of access</strong> — You can request a copy of your personal data.</li>
        <li><strong>Right to rectification</strong> — You can request correction of inaccurate data.</li>
        <li><strong>Right to erasure</strong> — You can request deletion of your data, subject to legal retention requirements.</li>
        <li><strong>Right to restrict processing</strong> — You can ask us to limit how we use your data.</li>
        <li><strong>Right to data portability</strong> — You can request your data in a structured, machine-readable format.</li>
        <li><strong>Right to object</strong> — You can object to processing based on legitimate interest.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        To exercise any of these rights, please contact us at
        <a href="mailto:ikian.dimitsana@gmail.com">ikian.dimitsana@gmail.com</a>.
        We will respond within 30 days.
      </p>

      <h2>9. Data Security</h2>
      <p>
        We take appropriate technical and organisational measures to protect your personal data
        against unauthorised access, loss, or misuse. This website is served over HTTPS to
        encrypt data in transit.
      </p>

      <h2>10. Supervisory Authority</h2>
      <p>
        If you believe your data protection rights have been violated, you have the right to
        lodge a complaint with the Hellenic Data Protection Authority (HDPA):
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Hellenic Data Protection Authority</strong><br>
        Kifisias 1-3, 115 23 Athens, Greece<br>
        Website: <a href="https://www.dpa.gr" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">www.dpa.gr</a><br>
        Phone: +30 210 647 5600
      </p>

      <h2>11. Changes to This Policy</h2>
      <p>
        We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. Any changes will be posted on this
        page with an updated "Last updated" date. We encourage you to review this page periodically.
      </p>

      <h2>12. Contact</h2>
      <p>
        For any questions regarding this Privacy Policy or how we handle your personal data,
        please contact us:
      </p>
      <p>
        Email: <a href="mailto:ikian.dimitsana@gmail.com">ikian.dimitsana@gmail.com</a><br>
        Phone: <a href="tel:+306973373560">+30 697 337 3560</a>
      </p>

      <!-- TODO: LEGAL REVIEW CHECKLIST
        - [ ] Confirm legal entity name and registration details
        - [ ] Confirm VAT / business registration number
        - [ ] Verify hosting provider's data processing agreement (DPA)
        - [ ] Confirm server log retention periods
        - [ ] Confirm guest registry retention requirements under Greek law
        - [ ] Confirm financial record retention periods under Greek tax law
        - [ ] Review CCTV section in Terms & Conditions — if CCTV is active, add CCTV
              processing details here and confirm DPIA has been completed
        - [ ] Confirm whether a Data Protection Officer (DPO) is required
        - [ ] Review with qualified legal professional before publication
      -->

    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .page-hero {
    background: var(--color-beige-light);
    padding: var(--space-3xl) 0 var(--space-2xl);
  }

  .page-hero h1 {
    letter-spacing: 0.05em;
  }

  .page-subtitle {
    color: var(--color-text-light);
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }

  .legal-container {
    max-width: 800px;
  }

  .legal-intro {
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    color: var(--color-text-light);
    line-height: 1.8;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-xl);
    padding-bottom: var(--space-xl);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-stone);
  }

  .legal-content h2 {
    margin-top: var(--space-xl);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-md);
    font-size: 1.3rem;
    color: var(--color-black);
  }

  .legal-content h3 {
    margin-top: var(--space-lg);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-sm);
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    color: var(--color-text);
  }

  .legal-content ul {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-md);
    padding-left: var(--space-lg);
  }

  .legal-content li {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-sm);
    line-height: 1.8;
    color: var(--color-text);
  }

  .legal-content p {
    line-height: 1.8;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-md);
  }
</style>
